## Docker

{% if choices.docker == "full" -%}
Mode: **everything in Docker**. `docker-compose.yml` has two services:

- `dev` (profile `dev`, stage `dev` of `Dockerfile`): mounts the project folder at `/app`, keeps `.venv` in the named volume `venv`, runs as user `app`, publishes `PLAYGROUND_PORT` and sets `PLAYGROUND_HOST=0.0.0.0`. It reads `.env` from the mounted folder (no `env_file`), so `.env` edits restart the bot like on the host. `docker compose up dev` runs `uv run poe dev`; `docker compose run --rm dev uv …` runs anything else. After changing dependencies run `docker compose run --rm dev uv sync`.
- `app`: the production image (see below), `docker compose up --build app`.
{%- else -%}
Mode: **Docker to run the app**. Development happens on the host with uv (`uv run poe dev`); Docker builds and runs the bot's production container.
{%- endif %}

- `Dockerfile` (multi-stage, `python:3.14-slim`, uv from `ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv`): installs the locked production dependencies (`uv sync --locked --no-dev`), then the runtime image copies `.venv` and `app/` and runs `python -m app run` as the non-root user `app`. `.env` is never copied into the image.
- `docker-compose.yml` passes `.env` to the `app` service (`env_file`), forces `APP_HOST=0.0.0.0`, publishes `APP_PORT` (health check and webhook) and restarts the bot unless stopped. `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` ({{ project.slug }}) names the stack.
- **Data:** `DOCKER_DATA` in `.env` decides where containers keep the SQLite files (`/app/data`): {% if choices.data == "local" %}**`./data`** — the project's `data/` folder is mounted (current setting); set `DOCKER_DATA=data` to use a Docker volume instead.{% else %}**`data`** — the named volume `{{ project.slug }}_data` (current setting); `docker compose down -v` deletes it. Set `DOCKER_DATA=./data` to keep the files in the project's `data/` folder instead.{% endif %}
- Commands: `docker compose up --build{% if choices.docker == "full" %} app{% endif %}`, `docker compose{% if choices.docker == "full" %} --profile dev{% endif %} logs -f`, `docker compose{% if choices.docker == "full" %} --profile dev{% endif %} down` (add `-v` to delete the volumes).
- The runtime image contains only `.venv` and `app/`. When the bot needs more files at runtime, add `COPY` lines to `Dockerfile` (and check `.dockerignore`). Runtime dependencies must be in `[project] dependencies`, not in the `dev` group.
{% endif %}
